				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1046,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Bridge VS Code dialog channels to Tauri's native dialog plugin\n\nAdd a native-host dialog bridge to IPCRendererShim that intercepts Electron-style dialog IPC channels (`nativeHost:showOpenDialog`, `vscode:showOpenDialog`, etc.) and translates them to Tauri's dialog API.\n\nThe implementation includes:\n- `handleDialogChannel` async handler for showOpenDialog, showSaveDialog, and showMessageBox\n- Translation functions converting Electron's `properties: ['openDirectory']` flags into Tauri's `{ directory: true }` format\n- Normalization of channel prefixes (nativeHost:, vscode:, native:) to extract the method name\n- Fallback responses matching VS Code's expected return types when Tauri dialog is unavailable\n\nAlso adds `TranslateOpenOptions` and `TranslateSaveOptions` to the NativeModulePolyfill to ensure consistent option translation in both the IPC layer and the dialog polyfill.\n\nWithout this, \"File → Open Folder\" silently fails because Tauri sees no `directory: true` flag and defaults to a file picker.\n\nAlso adds `Source/Utility/Tier.ts` providing Wind's mirror of Cocoon's tier feature-gating system using Vite's `import.meta.env.Tier<Capability>` substitution.",
			"SHA": "1740aad19970715df063945e1ad49e23a6848caf"
		},
